  "status": "feasibility_only_no_forward_returns",
  "hypothesis": "R257's realized P&L was dominated by repeated strength winners. A low 20-day maximum-single-day-return weakest link should retain quality and industry-relative leadership while avoiding lottery-like one-day spikes. This is distinct from a broad 5-day reversal and does not change R257's internal formula or portfolio constraints.",
  "selection_basis": "R257 passed all predictive, return and cost-stress gates but failed concentration C2/C3/C4 because top1/top3/top5 net P&L shares were 27.95%/64.08%/94.43%. R258's 20-day re-entry gate failed before returns because it left a median of only one fresh name, and R260's soft recency penalty reduced industry concentration but broke validation and recent returns. R261 tests a different mechanism: penalizing one-day lottery-like jumps rather than total short-term momentum. No R261 forward or strategy returns are read in this audit.",
